   "error": null,
   "response_text": "Found it \u2014 a textbook off-by-one. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**Cause:** In `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` guarded with `if quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:` where `BULK_THRESHOLD = 10`. The spec says \"10 or more\", but `>` demands strictly more, so exactly 10 units fell through to `return 0.0`. 11+ worked by accident.\n\n**Fix:** One character \u2014 `>` \u2192 `>=`:\n\n```python\nif quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD:\n    return round(quantity * unit_price * BULK_RATE, 2)\n```\n\nVerified: `bulk_discount(10, 25.0) == 12.5`, `9 -> 0.0`, `11 -> 13.75`, and the existing suite still passes (4 passed). Only the library source changed; no test files touched.\n\nDONE",
